ADDENDUM (post-run resolution, see verify_III_g78_c64_kps2.out):
The single FAIL above (G78 C64 certificate) was an artifact of THIS verifier's 60M-expansion
budget, not a sibling error. Follow-up run verify_III_g78_c64_kps2.py:
  * sibling's count_cycles_capped(A,64,cap=0) returns 1 in 0.2s;
  * witness extracted via their exact DFS logic is a VALID 64-cycle (64 distinct vertices,
    closed, all edges present);
  * this verifier's own finder also finds a valid C64 with seed=7 (33s).
=> G78 class 1 C64 EXISTS: sibling claim CONFIRMED.
FINAL VERDICT: ALL sibling numbers independently confirmed; zero substantive errors.
Reporting-level issues found (do not affect any verdict):
  1. Stage-2 'min #C16' table used only specimens[n][:3]; true minima over their own
     specimens are 726 at n=30 (not 736) and 852 at n=34 (not 855). Monotonic growth
     614@28 < 726@30 < 780@32 < 852@34 < 879@36 < 961@38 < 970@40 still holds.
  2. The '16x250K deep restarts' exist only for n=20/22/24 (dyadic_snark_cage_kps2.out);
     the announced n=26 deep run is absent (n=26 floor=1 rests on 8x60K; immaterial --
     n=26 > 0 is PROVEN by the exhaustive 23/23 census, all girth 3).
  3. 'C32 present' for all 577 girth-6 dihedral Cayley graphs was spot-checked on only 2
     specimens (b2b4 output shows c32=-1 inconclusive for the rest).
